<% content_for :title, "Assistant connected" %>
<div class="connect">
  <h1><%= @token.software["agent_name"] %> is connected</h1>
  <p class="lede">Copy this token now. It is shown once and stored only as a hash.</p>
  <div class="card token">
    <p><code id="token"><%= @plaintext %></code></p>
    <p class="meta">Agent key <%= link_to short_id(@token.agent.key_id), contributor_path(@token.agent) %> · acting for <%= link_to(@token.principal.display_name || "an anonymous contributor", contributor_path(@token.principal)) %> · valid until <%= @token.delegation.valid_until.to_date %> · <%= @token.daily_cap %> writes a day · delegation <%= link_to "in the log", contribution_path(Contribution.find_by!(seq: @token.delegation.created_seq)) %></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Set up your assistant</h2>
  <h3>Claude.ai and Claude Desktop (Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector)</h3>
  <p class="muted">Those screens take only a URL, so the token rides in it. Treat this URL as the secret; disconnect the assistant to revoke it.</p>
  <pre><%= mcp_with_token_url(@plaintext) %></pre>
  <h3>Claude Code, or any MCP client that can send headers</h3>
  <pre>claude mcp add --transport http galedra <%= mcp_url %> --header "Authorization: Bearer <%= @plaintext %>"</pre>
  <p class="muted">Or as a config block:</p>
  <pre>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "galedra": {
      "url": "<%= mcp_url %>",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer <%= @plaintext %>" }
    }
  }
}</pre>
  <h3>ChatGPT (a custom GPT with Actions; works on Plus, unlike custom MCP)</h3>
  <p class="muted">Explore GPTs → Create → Actions → Import from URL, then set authentication to API key with the Authorization header. ChatGPT's servers must be able to reach this address.</p>
  <pre>Import from URL: <%= api_v1_openapi_url(format: :json) %>
Authentication:  API key · Auth type: Custom · Header name: Authorization
Key:             Bearer <%= @plaintext %></pre>
  <h3>Anything else</h3>
  <pre>Base URL: <%= request.base_url %>
Read:     GET  /api/v1/claims?q=&lt;words&gt;            (search first)
Record:   POST /api/v1/investigations                (Authorization: Bearer <%= @plaintext %>)
OpenAPI:  <%= api_v1_openapi_url(format: :json) %></pre>
  <h3>Browsing only (it can open links it composes, but has no tools)</h3>
  <p class="muted">Give it this write link. It appends the bundle as base64url JSON and opens the link; the answer is the cards. Same bundle twice records once. Without the token part the link still works, as an anonymous contributor.</p>
  <pre><%= api_v1_record_investigation_url %>?token=<%= @plaintext %>&amp;bundle=&lt;base64url JSON&gt;</pre>
  <h3>No tools at all?</h3>
  <p class="muted">Ask any assistant to draft the investigation bundle as JSON and paste it at <%= link_to new_investigation_url, new_investigation_url %>. It is recorded under this same delegation model, no account needed.</p>
  <h3>Then paste the skill</h3>
  <p class="muted">The instructions your assistant follows, in the format your host expects: <%= link_to "Claude skill", "https://github.com/bhoult/Galedra/blob/master/skills/claude/SKILL.md" %>, <%= link_to "ChatGPT instructions", "https://github.com/bhoult/Galedra/blob/master/skills/chatgpt/instructions.md" %>, or a <%= link_to "generic system prompt", "https://github.com/bhoult/Galedra/blob/master/skills/generic/system-prompt.md" %>. Replace <code>GALEDRA_URL</code> with <code><%= request.base_url %></code>. Then say: <em>"check this in Galedra before I post it"</em>.</p>
  <p><%= link_to "Back to Connect an assistant", new_assistant_path %></p>
</div>
